  16:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/rsa_alt_helpers.c **** 
  17:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/rsa_alt_helpers.c **** /*
  18:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/rsa_alt_helpers.c ****  * Compute RSA prime factors from public and private exponents
  19:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/rsa_alt_helpers.c ****  *
  20:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/rsa_alt_helpers.c ****  * Summary of algorithm:
  21:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/rsa_alt_helpers.c ****  * Setting F := lcm(P-1,Q-1), the idea is as follows:
  22:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/rsa_alt_helpers.c ****  *
  23:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/rsa_alt_helpers.c ****  * (a) For any 1 <= X < N with gcd(X,N)=1, we have X^F = 1 modulo N, so X^(F/2)
  24:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/rsa_alt_helpers.c ****  *     is a square root of 1 in Z/NZ. Since Z/NZ ~= Z/PZ x Z/QZ by CRT and the
  25:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/rsa_alt_helpers.c ****  *     square roots of 1 in Z/PZ and Z/QZ are +1 and -1, this leaves the four
  26:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/rsa_alt_helpers.c ****  *     possibilities X^(F/2) = (+-1, +-1). If it happens that X^(F/2) = (-1,+1)
  27:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/rsa_alt_helpers.c ****  *     or (+1,-1), then gcd(X^(F/2) + 1, N) will be equal to one of the prime
  28:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/rsa_alt_helpers.c ****  *     factors of N.
  29:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/rsa_alt_helpers.c ****  *
  30:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/rsa_alt_helpers.c ****  * (b) If we don't know F/2 but (F/2) * K for some odd (!) K, then the same
  31:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/rsa_alt_helpers.c ****  *     construction still applies since (-)^K is the identity on the set of
  32:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/rsa_alt_helpers.c ****  *     roots of 1 in Z/NZ.
  33:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/rsa_alt_helpers.c ****  *
  34:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/rsa_alt_helpers.c ****  * The public and private key primitives (-)^E and (-)^D are mutually inverse
  35:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/rsa_alt_helpers.c ****  * bijections on Z/NZ if and only if (-)^(DE) is the identity on Z/NZ, i.e.
  36:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/rsa_alt_helpers.c ****  * if and only if DE - 1 is a multiple of F, say DE - 1 = F * L.
  37:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/rsa_alt_helpers.c ****  * Splitting L = 2^t * K with K odd, we have
  38:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/rsa_alt_helpers.c ****  *
  39:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/rsa_alt_helpers.c ****  *   DE - 1 = FL = (F/2) * (2^(t+1)) * K,
  40:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/rsa_alt_helpers.c ****  *
  41:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/rsa_alt_helpers.c ****  * so (F / 2) * K is among the numbers
  42:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/rsa_alt_helpers.c ****  *
  43:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/rsa_alt_helpers.c ****  *   (DE - 1) >> 1, (DE - 1) >> 2, ..., (DE - 1) >> ord
  44:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/rsa_alt_helpers.c ****  *
  45:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/rsa_alt_helpers.c ****  * where ord is the order of 2 in (DE - 1).
  46:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/rsa_alt_helpers.c ****  * We can therefore iterate through these numbers apply the construction
  47:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/rsa_alt_helpers.c ****  * of (a) and (b) above to attempt to factor N.
GAS LISTING /tmp/ccQCYXyK.s 			page 2


  48:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/rsa_alt_helpers.c ****  *
